Accounting-regime flag is a capability proxy: US firms report under US-GAAP (LIFO permitted), non-US firms under IFRS (LIFO prohibited). The dataset does not record the actual inventory-costing method, so 'lifo_capable' marks only what the regime allows. Under LIFO, reported inventory and DIO can be understated versus FIFO/IFRS peers, so cross-country DIO levels are not perfectly comparable.
